-- tweaked and enhanced old razing logic so we that we (i.e. AI (excluding the barbarian player itself, but as for cities applies more or less to all cities even non-barbarian ones if i'm not mistaken anyways et) players but anyways etc) now raze cities in the early (as of now first 120 turns adjusted to game speed anyways etc) game if they are not close enough to make it worth the early investment. This helps not spread our military forces (which was a major issue in base advciv when it happened, often with most troops being in the new captured faraway city while core ones would be less defended, hopefully much saner and stronger razing now if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc) and scrace economy ressources (city maintenance would be increased per city, pop is generally low in these cities plus the time to build improvements or/and culture or such there, plus the city maintenance in the city itself, etc) so that they stay focused. Indirectly, it may often lead to less fog busting so more barbarians, which is good since it's far from us so will weaken our rivals if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc. As a result of this, AI should be much stronger in the early game, and hopefully no longer split in two making it much easier to defeat (especially if most forces are in the new city). See [64 - (Greatly enhanced) AI not razing faraway cities at captures - now we raze them if we are in the early game and they are not close enough, thanks to changes and tweaks in CvPlayerAI::AI_conquerCity anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#64---greatly-enhanced-ai-not-razing-faraway-cities-at-captures---now-we-raze-them-if-we-are-in-the-early-game-and-they-are-not-close-enough-thanks-to-changes-and-tweaks-in-cvplayeraiai_conquercity-anyways-etc) for details anyways etc.
+- tweaked and enhanced old razing logic so we that we (i.e. AI (excluding the barbarian player itself, but as for cities applies more or less to all cities even non-barbarian ones if i'm not mistaken anyways et) players but anyways etc) now raze cities in the early (as of now first 120 turns adjusted to game speed anyways etc) game if they are not close enough to make it worth the early investment, in `CvPlayerAI::AI_conquerCity`. This helps not spread our military forces (which was a major issue in base advciv when it happened, often with most troops being in the new captured faraway city while core ones would be less defended, hopefully much saner and stronger razing now if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc) and scrace economy ressources (city maintenance would be increased per city, pop is generally low in these cities plus the time to build improvements or/and culture or such there, plus the city maintenance in the city itself, etc) so that they stay focused. Indirectly, it may often lead to less fog busting so more barbarians, which is good since it's far from us so will weaken our rivals if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc. As a result of this, AI should be much stronger in the early game, and hopefully no longer split in two making it much easier to defeat (especially if most forces are in the new city). See [64 - (Greatly enhanced) AI not razing faraway cities at captures - now we raze them if we are in the early game and they are not close enough, thanks to changes and tweaks in CvPlayerAI::AI_conquerCity anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#64---greatly-enhanced-ai-not-razing-faraway-cities-at-captures---now-we-raze-them-if-we-are-in-the-early-game-and-they-are-not-close-enough-thanks-to-changes-and-tweaks-in-cvplayeraiai_conquercity-anyways-etc) for details anyways etc.
 - Fixed and enhanced the issue of AI overbuilding defenders in the early game. It now tries (at least in theory in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` anyways etc) to replace the unit to build with an offense of versatile leaning. Typically, this means less longbowmen and more spearmen, camel archers, axemen, etc. We avoid to produce excess siege (in particular trebuchets-like units anyways etc) since they are not versatile enough to be used at defense and offense especially by the AI but anyways etc. The focus and assumption is we'll do good enough early where power differences are still not that great and gains potentially important to make. We also as of now favour civ-specific units (e.g. an egyptian war chariot rather than a horse archer if i'm not mistaken anyways etc) most times. If no good unit candidate is found, we attempt to hijack the unitai of the defensive unit (e.g. a longbowman with attack or attack_city or counter instead of city_defense). Results are very impressive!! They don't seem to always apply or entirely apply, but it does seem like most rivals have significantly less longbowmen and a more varied composition, and sometimes the difference is massive. For example in a run, hatshepsut ai went from +/- 30+ longbowmen for +/- 6 cities at turn 130 to 32 war chariots (plus camel archers for some reason etc), while some ais had often few, sometimes many longbowmen for some reason. Still, overall the seemingly more versatile compositions for all AI players, hopefully helps them better transition into an offensive middle game strategy and not be stuck with useless excess defenders. This should help boxed in players in particular, but also any AI with excess unit, after quite minimal defense needs are met (offense units can defend then as well and are more versatile if i am not mistaken but anyways etc, the varied composition also indirectly helps counter picks to invade us (like building spearmen vs chariots, or axes vs swords, hopefully, but anyways etc)). See originally changes in [53.2 - (Fixed and enhanced) Joao AI building way too many defenders (36 longbowmen at turn 130!! Almost all with UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE or similar) while being boxed in with only 3 cities, instead of making about half of these offense units or versatile ones to punish overextending thin neighbour, fixed by having an early phase "we have expectedly too few cities at this stage of the game, no need to overbuild anymore denders at this stage of the game, switch to offense or versatile UNITAI rather" and "our military composition has way too many defender UNITAIs, switch to offense or versatile UNITAIs", which seemingly fix the issue anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#532---fixed-and-enhanced-joao-ai-building-way-too-many-defenders-36-longbowmen-at-turn-130-almost-all-with-unitai_city_defense-or-similar-while-being-boxed-in-with-only-3-cities-instead-of-making-about-half-of-these-offense-units-or-versatile-ones-to-punish-overextending-thin-neighbour-fixed-by-having-an-early-phase-we-have-expectedly-too-few-cities-at-this-stage-of-the-game-no-need-to-overbuild-anymore-denders-at-this-stage-of-the-game-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitai-rather-and-our-military-composition-has-way-too-many-defender-unitais-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitais-which-seemingly-fix-the-issue-anyways-etc) and then a more refined and enhanced, as of now final version of these in [53.2.2 (Seemingly greatly enhanced) AI overproducing defenders early on, especially longbowmen but not only, replaced with an early produce more versatile units especially civ-specific ones when defended enough (at least in theory anyways etc) in CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#5322-seemingly-greatly-enhanced-ai-overproducing-defenders-early-on-especially-longbowmen-but-not-only-replaced-with-an-early-produce-more-versatile-units-especially-civ-specific-ones-when-defended-enough-at-least-in-theory-anyways-etc-in-cvcityaiai_chooseunit-anyways-etc) anyways etc.
 - Tremendously improved AI overbuilding trebuchets in particular but more generally siege units, especially when it is bad like being weaker (trebuchets are useless and very hammer inefficient if not strictly to attack city tiles, catapults or cannons or such are also not too versatile or/and used correctly by AI to defend for example). Used various conditions in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` to try to make siege units production as minimal as possible, up to none at all if needed, but if other conditions are met but anyways etc hopefully not too low (a bit low as of now but much better than before when it was too strong). As a result, AIs should have a more varied offensive stack composition, as well as being better at defense when weaker, as seems the case in autoplay test i ran at a glance but anyways etc. See for details [53.3 (Tremendously Improved) AI overbuilding siege units, in particular trebuchets but not only, where they are detrimental to do build, in particular when weaker but not only anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#533-tremendously-improved-ai-overbuilding-siege-units-in-particular-trebuchets-but-not-only-where-they-are-detrimental-to-do-build-in-particular-when-weaker-but-not-only-anyways-etc). Update: since then, relaxed siege thresholds in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` and in the fallback unit if no production code as well in `CvCity::doTurn`: slightly relaxed them before renaissance, and relaxed them extra more if we have key strategic bonus (as of now iron, copper, horse, camel, elephants) as siege units may help us do a successful longbow rush or such if we fit the other offense conditions to produce them if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc, and heavily relaxed them at renaissance+ as cannons as a viable alternative to a defender, especially if we have no mounted bonus and no access to muskets yet, overbuilding pikemen against cuirassiers is useless, ineffective, and will bankrupt us sooner. More generally also allows more varied stacks compositions and much better results ingame for some AIs it seems that had the issue of dying due to having too much pikemen and keeping to build them when cannons and later siege units are available and much stronger / more effective, but check to be sure anyways etc.
